Let me back up just a tad and discuss the current progress of offense
vs. defense.  Depressingly, killing people seems a lot easier than
defending yourself these days, and I don't see that changing.  This
raises concerns for the future.

How can you protect yourself in an age of cheap nukes and bioweapons?
My only answer is:  you RUN AND HIDE.  My mental image is of a lot of
extended-family-size self-sufficient colonies, shielded against
radiation leakage, "hiding" in the depths of space.  They communicate
using cheap throwaway relay probes so as not to give away their
positions.  Trade is mostly in the form of information, which can be
traded safely, although buying supplies from a company with a good and
long-standing reputation is a possibility.

I'm not all that happy with this scenario, but at least it's not one of
total destruction.  It seems to follow naturally from two assumptions
which I believe hold in reality:  offense is easy when you can see your
target, but hiding without detection is feasible.

